        },
        rules: {
          objective: "Be the first player to meld all 13 cards in your hand by forming sets and runs. The winner 'calls up' and scores zero; other players score penalty points for remaining cards.",
          gameplay: "1. **Drawing**: Each turn, draw either the top card of the stock or the top discard. 2. **Melding**: If you can form valid melds meeting the initial point requirement, lay them face-up. 3. **Building**: After initial meld, add cards to any existing meld (yours or opponents'). 4. **Discarding**: End turn by discarding one card face-up.",
          keyRules: [
            'Initial meld must total at least 40 or 51 points (house rule)',
            'Sets: 3-4 cards of same rank, all different suits (no duplicates)',
            'Runs: 3+ consecutive cards of same suit; Aces are high only (A-K-Q valid, 3-2-A invalid)',
            'Jokers are wild and can substitute any card in a meld',
            'Jokers in hand at end of play count as 15 penalty points',
            'Building: After initial meld, add cards to extend existing melds on table',
            'Cannot build more than 2 cards to same end of a run in one turn',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        strategy: {
          basic: 'Prioritize reaching the initial meld threshold (40/51 points) as quickly as possible. Use high-value cards (Aces, Face cards) to meet this requirement efficiently.',
          intermediate: 'Joker Management: Hold Jokers until you can use them in a meldâ€”15 penalty points is severe. Watch for opportunities to exchange for Jokers on the table. Track which cards have been discarded to calculate drawing odds.',
          advanced: "Defensive Discarding: Avoid discarding cards that could help opponents complete their initial meld or extend their existing melds. The 'Late Meld' strategy: Hold back small melds to prevent opponents from building on them. Calculate exactly when to 'call up' based on opponent hand sizes.",
          tips: [
            'Three Aces = 33 pointsâ€”more than half the 51-point requirement',
            "Don't hold Jokers too longâ€”the 15-point penalty can eliminate you",
            'Watch opponent discards to deduce what suits they are collecting',
            'In sets with Jokers, you need both missing suits to exchangeâ€”plan accordingly',
          ],
